    description: "Swift meta[\"arg_labels\"] keeps a backquoted label's backquotes, so a call that writes the label without them does not resolve. Given `func f(\\`default\\` x: Int)`, the call `s.f(default: 1)` is left unresolved; spell the label `dflt` and the same call binds. Call edges only: no stable id moves (PR 5's label hashing already strips the backquotes for the id).\n\nFound by PR 5 agent 1 (WI-lonoh). Repro: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr5/lonoh/residual_fixtures/R.swift."  # 3395
